Subject: Re: When performing multigroup analysis, are the factor scores standardized for each group?
Message-ID: <EFCkjeLrLEk.-IRIk1SXCwAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <EFCkjeLrLEk.e14NyBtDDAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
References: <EFCkjeLrLEk._f_gesZBDAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com> <EFCkjeLrLEk.e14NyBtDDAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/EFCkjeLrLEk/m/-IRIk1SXCwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You constrain across groups by giving the same label.

Something like:

LS =~ LS1 + c(lam2, lam2, lam2) * LS2 +
          c(lam3, lam3, lam3) * LS3 +
          c(lam4, lam4, lam4) * LS4 +
          c(lam5, lam5, lam5) * LS5 +
          c(lam6, lam6, lam6) * LS6

(There's also the measurementinvariance() function in semTools, see http://users.ugent.be/~yrosseel/lavaan/multiplegroup6Dec2012.pdf ).

