From: u3fe90052fbf2f899 at groups.google.com (Terrence Jorgensen)
Date: Fri, 24 Aug 2018 08:05:30 +0000
Subject: Re: lavTestLRT using Yuan-Bentler correction
Message-ID: <yjv3darveqs.hrkNGXbABgAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <yjv3darveqs.Ls61FZk4EAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
References: <yjv3darveqs.Ls61FZk4EAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/yjv3darveqs/m/hrkNGXbABgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> the standard anova or LavTestLRT function still uses the ML estimated Chi-square values. Why? And how can I change this?

That is what it is supposed to do.  A scaled chi-squared-difference test is not the difference between two robust chi-squared values.  Like the scaling of the individual models' chi-squareds, the (naïve) chi-squared difference needs to be scaled.  You can see some details here:

https://www.statmodel.com/chidiff.shtml

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
UvA web page: http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

