> Do you know if the same hard limitations would apply using Bayesian estimation?

Unlike these frequentist methods, Bayes is not built on asymptotic theory, although more data always helps to draw more confident conclusions.  If there are convergence problems with MCMC estimation, you can help it out by specifying more informative priors, but make sure to perform a sensitivity analysis with different priors to see how much your results depend on them.  Hopefully you will find the blavaan package helpful.

